# Data import — real company data (source spreadsheets) and generated JSON output.
# Never commit either: the .xlsx are confidential GSM data and output/ is derived.
#
# Full lifecycle of data-import/source/ (see data-import/README.md):
#   1. The .xlsx are copied by hand onto the server, only when an import is due.
#   2. The import scripts (npm run import:*) read them.
#   3. They are deleted from disk immediately afterwards.
# They are never versioned and never `git add`ed — not even briefly — and they must
# never sit on the server between one import and the next. Once one reaches a commit,
# getting it out means rewriting history on every remote.
#
# Removing or narrowing the next line aborts the import scripts on purpose:
# data-import/source-guard.ts re-checks it with `git check-ignore` before every read.
data-import/source/
data-import/output/
